The kachō-e illustration pipeline in this directory (pregen.py, cutout.py,
prompt.template.md, species-notes.json and the scripts around them) is adapted
from AvianVisitors by Teagan Warner:

    https://github.com/Twarner491/AvianVisitors

AvianVisitors is licensed under Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-
ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0), and so is everything in this
directory, along with the illustration files it produces (the seeded art is
theirs; the generated art is a derivative made with their prompt approach).

    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/

In short: you may use, share and adapt this pipeline and its art for
non-commercial purposes, as long as you credit AvianVisitors and release your
adaptations under the same license. The Edo-period style reference prints
(Ohara Koson, Yoshida Hiroshi) are public domain.

The rest of the bird-listener repository (the display service, the detection
node setup, the laptop CLI) is separate original work under the MIT License in
the repository root.
